   "design": "Patrons pay fines online in their account or at the self-service kiosk, and payments post to the library system ({OTHER}) automatically, so fewer fines are taken and booked at the desk. Each week the technician reviews the list of unpaid fines; once checked, reminders go out by e-mail from the system instead of letters. Waivers are recorded with a reason code. Handling complaints stays with the technician.",
   "previous_blocker": "Fines were paid in cash at the desk, booked by hand and chased by letter.",
   "enabler_now": "Library systems take online payments and send scheduled notices.",
   "still_hard": "Some patrons only pay cash.",
   "human_edge": "Waiving a fine for a family that is struggling.",
